CREATED:20261103T191711Z
DESCRIPTION:The RePlant team is co-hosting our second workshop "Indigenous
  Economies of Care: Food sharing\, reading circles\, and seed saving " wi
 th the Native American Indigenous Student Association (NAISA) at Duke on 
 Saturday\, November 14th\, 1-4pm at Duke Campus Farm's Southeastern Ameri
 can Indian Garden.\n\nThis is a gathering centered around the gift econom
 ies of Native peoples with an intercultural potluck\, a discussion of wor
 ks by Robin Wall Kimmerer\, and a seed saving demonstration.\n\nWe invite
  participants to bring food from your culture or homeland.\n\nTo join the
  RePlant working group and hear about future events\, please sign up here
  https://lists.duke.edu/sympa/subscribe/replant.\n\nRePlant and Compostin
 g Theory have joined forces to amplify conversations in the plant humanit
 ies\, and to consider\, and work towards\, ecological care in practice. T
 his series is supported by the Franklin Humanities Institute\, Duke's Off
 ice of Climate and Sustainability\, the Revaluing Care Lab\, and the Duke
  Campus Farm.\n\nRSVP here: https://www.eventbrite.com/e/indigenous-econo
 mies-of-care-tickets-2004122525423?aff=oddtdtcreator
DURATION:PT3H
DTSTAMP:20261103T191711Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20261114T130000
LAST-MODIFIED:20261103T191711Z
