CREATED:20260714T175641Z
DESCRIPTION:Explore three centuries of musical innovation as faculty violi
 nist Gabriel Richard presents "The Three Bs: Bach\, Bartók\, Boulez-Persp
 ectives on Form from the Baroque to the Contemporary."\n\nThe program tra
 ces the evolution of musical form through a violin transcription of Bach'
 s BWV 542\, Bartók's Sonata for Solo Violin\, Boulez's Anthèmes I\, and B
 ach's Partita No. 2 for Solo Violin. Moving from the intricate architectu
 re of the Baroque to the bold musical languages of the 20th century\, the
  recital reveals striking connections among three composers whose works c
 ontinually challenge and redefine the possibilities of sound.\n\nThis eve
 nt is free and open to the public. All are welcome.
DURATION:PT2H
DTSTAMP:20260901T150548Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20261114T200000
LAST-MODIFIED:20260901T150548Z
