DESCRIPTION:An inventive retelling of a Jacobean drama\, Jen Silverman's s
 harp\, subversive fable debates how much our souls are worth when hope is
  hard to come by. The Duke University Department of Theater Studies produ
 cess two Mainstage plays each year in fall and spring semesters under the
  direction of a faculty member or visiting artist. Students participate i
 n these productions on stage and behind the scenes.This show is part of W
 e the People: A Duke and Durham Initiative.
DURATION:PT2H
