CREATED:20261104T150011Z
DESCRIPTION:GAMA RAYS & CHATINOS HOY Y SIEMPRE\n5:30 PM. Serenade with MAR
 IACHI TORO \n6:00 pm - 7:00 pm | Indigenous South America\, Mexico\, and 
 the U.S.\n*Ticketed event (REQUEST TICKETS TO: mlr34@duke.edu\, las@duke.
 edu)\n \nGama Rays. Dir. J.J. Ortiz\, Gia Jiménez Huamán. 2026. Colombia.
  15 min. Kagaba\, with English subtitles.\nThe softer voice of Saga María
 \, a female Indigenous philosopher\, shares the embodied knowledge and pr
 actice of transforming natural fibers into Kogi archives. A rare moment w
 ith one of the most traditional Indigenous peoples of the Sierra Nevada d
 e Santa Marta\, and probably the most sustainable people on earth. \n\nFo
 r the Indigenous Peoples of the Sierra Nevada de Gonawindúa\, known in Sp
 anish as the Sierra Nevada de Santa Marta in the north of Colombia\, weav
 ing the traditional mochila (GAMA/backpack) represents the act of creatin
 g the world\, of recreating life\; as such\, this is the work of the Indi
 genous women.\n\nThis short is produced by P'alante Producciones\, DukeEn
 gage Colombia\, and the Teyku Community of Sierra Nevada de Santa Marta.\
 n\nProduced by Miguel Rojas Sotelo.\n\n\nWith the presence of the filmmak
 ers\n\n\n\nChatinos hoy y siempre / NeqA TnyaE NiC QoE SaA TykwiE. 2026. 
 Dir. Gabriela Badillo. 68 Voces 68 Corazones  (MX/USA). Animation.  Chati
 no with English subtitles. 4 min\nA manifesto of the resilience of the Ch
 atino communities in Oaxaca and their diasporas in Durham\, North Carolin
 a. By living\, working\, and embodying their language\, Chatinos survive 
 the multiple waves of oppression\, coloniality\, fear\, and displacement.
  An ode to their culture and traditions\, yesterday\, today\, and forever
 .\n\nThis is the latest animation\, number forty-three of sixty-eight sto
 ries that rescue and share Mexico's linguistic and cultural diversity. \n
 \n*With the presence of the filmmaker and members of the Chatino Communit
 y of Durham.\n\nFollowed by a Reception
DURATION:PT2H
DTSTAMP:20261104T150011Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20261115T173000
LAST-MODIFIED:20261104T150011Z
