CONTACT;X-BEDEWORK-UID=00f1fcdb-0f068baf-010f-068baf83-00000004:None
CREATED:20261109T204905Z
DESCRIPTION:Anna Murray Douglass was a freedom-fighter\, strategist\, and 
 revolutionary whose contributions have too often been overshadowed by tho
 se of her husband\, Frederick Douglass. Join author Celeste-Marie Bernier
  with director\, writer\, producer\, and Duke alumnus Charles Randolph-Wr
 ight ("American Prophet: Frederick Douglass in His Own Words")\, and Doug
 lass family member Kenneth B. Morris\, Jr.\, for a conversation about "An
 na Murray Douglass: Biography of a Revolutionary" (Duke University Press\
 , 2026) the first standalone biography devoted to her life and work.\n\nD
 rawing on more than thirty years of archival research and collaboration w
 ith family descendants\, Bernier reveals Anna Murray Douglass's leadershi
 p in the struggle against slavery\, racism\, and white supremacy-from hel
 ping secure Frederick Douglass's self-liberation to making the family's h
 omes centers of Underground Railroad activity. The book challenges famili
 ar accounts of individual heroism to illuminate a family's multigeneratio
 nal commitment to freedom.
DURATION:PT1H
DTSTAMP:20261109T204905Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20261116T140000
LAST-MODIFIED:20261109T204905Z
